#Install pycharm in window 


#Open your web browser.
-Go to the official PyCharm website:
-PyCharm Downloads
-Choose the edition:
  Community Edition – Free and suitable for most learners and Python developers.
  Professional Edition – Paid, with additional features for web development, databases, and scientific tools.
#Run the Installer
-Open the downloaded .exe installer.
-If Windows asks for permission, click Yes.
-Click Next.
#Choose Installation Options

You can leave the defaults, but these options are commonly recommended:

-Create Desktop Shortcut (64-bit)
-Add "Open Folder as Project" (optional)
-Add PyCharm to PATH (optional but useful)
-Associate .py files with PyCharm (optional)

Click Next.

#Install
-Click Install.
-Wait for the installation to finish.
-Click Finish
